# Build output is not committed.
#
# The trust model requires that the bytes running in a merchant's page are traceable to public
# source by someone who does not trust us. npm provenance provides exactly that: publishing
# attaches a signed attestation binding the tarball to the commit and the workflow run that
# produced it, logged publicly and verifiable with `npm audit signatures`. Committing `dist/`
# would be a weaker form of the same claim, since it asks the reader to trust that this
# repository's history is honest.
#
# That claim was unbacked while this code lived in a private repository. It is backed now, which
# makes this rule load-bearing rather than tidy — see VERIFYING.md for what a reader is expected
# to be able to do, none of which involves a checked-in bundle.
dist/

# Generated by `build.mjs` from `LICENSE` at the root, so npm packs it from the package
# directory. One editable copy, no drift; the build refuses to publish without it.
sdk/LICENSE
